  "key_findings": "[提出: 用戶, 執行: Claude] K917 examines whether Taiwan's ex-dividend season (June-August) exhibits systematically different volatility for 0050.TW (Taiwan 50 ETF). Using 20 years of data (2006-2026, 4217 daily observations), we compute monthly realized volatility and test for seasonal patterns. \n\nCore finding: The Welch's t-test comparing Jun-Aug vs other months shows t=-1.033 (p=0.3028), indicating NO statistically significant difference. Summer mean RV = 0.1691, other months = 0.1846. Cohen's d = -0.1195 (negligible). \n\nVIX control regression: When VIX is included, summer dummy becomes insignificant (t=-0.103), confirming VIX sufficiency — the ex-dividend season effect is fully absorbed by VIX. \n\nYear-by-year stability: summer vol higher in only 9/17 years (53%), showing inconsistent pattern. Permutation test p=0.4890. \n\nPractical implication: Investors do NOT need to adjust VT strategy parameters for ex-dividend season — VIX already captures any seasonal volatility changes. The 8.63/VIX strategy naturally adjusts via VIX, requiring no seasonal override.",
  "experiment_id": "K917",
  "title": "Taiwan Ex-Dividend Season Volatility Effect",
  "data_source": "yfinance (0050.TW, 0056.TW, ^VIX)",
  "sample_period": "2009-01-05 to 2026-03-31",
  "n_observations": 4217,
  "methodology": [
    "Monthly realized volatility (daily std × sqrt(252))",
    "Welch's t-test (summer vs other months)",
    "Mann-Whitney U test (non-parametric)",
    "Kruskal-Wallis test (all 12 months)",
    "Permutation test (5000 reps)",
    "OLS regression with VIX control (HC1 robust SE)",
    "Ex-dividend day event study ([-10,+10] window)",
    "Fill gap analysis",
    "Sub-period analysis (pre/post 2015)"
  ],
  "references": [
    "Lakonishok & Vermaelen (1986): Tax-induced trading around ex-dividend days, JFE"
  ],
  "limitations": [
    "0050.TW is an ETF (diversified) — individual stock effects are diluted",
